{"availability":"available","full":"bakodramane/DATA_CLEANING_SYNTAX_APP","name":"DATA_CLEANING_SYNTAX_APP","description":"Offline-first, open-source tool for survey statisticians to turn codebooks and metadata into transparent data-cleaning, validation and imputation syntax for SPSS, Stata, R and Python.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-30T14:04:58Z","updated":"2026-06-04T14:31:23Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://bakodramane.github.io/DATA_CLEANING_SYNTAX_APP/","topics":["data-cleaning","ddi","imputation","metadata","microdata","official-statistics","offline-first","pwa","python","r","spss","stata","survey-data"],"demo":"https://bakodramane.github.io/DATA_CLEANING_SYNTAX_APP/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:54.882Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:54.882Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T05:44:54.882Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T05:44:54.882Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An open-source, offline-first web app for turning survey metadata into reviewable data-cleaning syntax.","The app is for official statisticians, survey operations teams, data managers, and analysts who need a transparent first draft of cleaning and imputation syntax from a data dictionary. It does not clean data directly and it does not execute generated scripts. Instead, it builds a language-neutral Cleaning Plan from imported metadata, then renders syntax that a human analyst can review, adapt, and run in their own statistical environment.","The wizard includes concise reviewer guidance at each step, next-action empty states, separated import and validation warnings, and export descriptions that explain what each downloaded file is for. These usability cues are intended for non-technical statisticians without changing the statistical engine."],"features":["Documentation/reporting only: labels, metadata tr